{
    "background_story": "Zaniyah was a free-spirited artist known for her vibrant and expressive paintings. She fell in love with tempera paint in her early childhood, mesmerized by the way the colors blended and swirled on the paper. As she grew older, Zaniyah's passion for tempera only intensified, and she began experimenting with new techniques and styles. Her artwork often featured bold, abstract shapes and colors that seemed to dance across the canvas. Zaniyah's use of tempera paint was not just about creating visually stunning pieces, but also about tapping into her emotions and inner world. She believed that the fluidity and unpredictability of tempera allowed her to tap into her subconscious mind, resulting in truly unique and authentic works of art. Zaniyah's art studio was a kaleidoscope of colors, with tempera paint splatters covering every surface, a testament to her creative genius.",
